    {
      "id": "129c1d816679-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "(2 8 &divide; 2 5 ) 2 is equal to:",
      "questionHtml": "(2<sup>8</sup>&nbsp;&divide; 2<sup>5</sup>)<sup>2</sup> is equal to:",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "64",
          "html": "64"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "8/5",
          "html": "8/5"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "32",
          "html": "32"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "128",
          "html": "128"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concept:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">According to the surds and indices rule-</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;(a<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">m</span>)<sup>n</sup> =&nbsp;a<sup>m &times; n</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Using the theorem stated above, we get-</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">(2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">8</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;&divide;&nbsp;2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">5</span><span style=\"\">)</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span>=&nbsp;<span style=\"\">(2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">8</span><span style=\"\">)</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&divide;</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"\">(2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">5</span><span style=\"\">)</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; <span style=\"\">2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">16&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&divide;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">2</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">10</span>&nbsp;= 2<sup>6</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 64</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">The value of the expression is 64.</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "129c1d816679-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "\\(\\frac{(27)^4}{(125)^2}\\) &divide; \\(\\left\\{\\left(\\frac{5}{9}\\right)^{-2}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^6\\right\\} \\) is equal to :",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(27)^4}{(125)^2}\\)</span>&nbsp;&divide;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left\\{\\left(\\frac{5}{9}\\right)^{-2}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^6\\right\\} \\)</span>&nbsp;is equal to :",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "125",
          "html": "125"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "225",
          "html": "225"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "289",
          "html": "289"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "300",
          "html": "300"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p>(27)<sup>4</sup>/ (125)<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= 3<sup>12</sup>/5<sup>6</sup></p>\n\n<p>(5/9)<sup>-2</sup>&nbsp;= (9/5)<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(27)^4}{(125)^2}\\)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;/&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\left\\{\\left(\\frac{5}{9}\\right)^{-2}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^6\\right\\} \\)</span>&nbsp;= (<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">3</span><span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">12</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">/5</span><span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">6</span>) /&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">(9/5)</span><span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;&times; (3/5)<sup>6</sup></p>\n\n<p>= 3<sup>12</sup>&nbsp;&nbsp;&times; 5<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;&times; 5<sup>6</sup>&nbsp;/ 3<sup>4</sup>&nbsp;&times; 3<sup>6</sup>&nbsp;= 3<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;&times; 5<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= 225</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hence, The Correct Answer is option 2.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
